From 4216766763680c90841804813aaf812740397bd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LGA1150 <9155358+LGA1150@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:12:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: eip93 - reject non-word authentication tag sizes

The SA digest-length field counts 32-bit words. Accepting an arbitrary
byte length silently rounds it down, so a requested 13-byte tag programs
only 12 bytes while request accounting still uses 13.

Reject lengths the hardware field cannot represent before changing the
transform or SA record. The AEAD core already checks zero and lengths
above the algorithm's maximum.

Signed-off-by: LGA1150 <9155358+LGA1150@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 eip93-aead.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/eip93-aead.c b/eip93-aead.c
index 9704f77..4a59eac 100644
--- a/eip93-aead.c
+++ b/eip93-aead.c
@@ -144,6 +144,9 @@ static int eip93_aead_setauthsize(struct crypto_aead *ctfm,
 	struct crypto_tfm *tfm = crypto_aead_tfm(ctfm);
 	struct eip93_crypto_ctx *ctx = crypto_tfm_ctx(tfm);
 
+	if (!IS_ALIGNED(authsize, sizeof(u32)))
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	ctx->authsize = authsize;
 	ctx->sa_record->sa_cmd0_word &= ~EIP93_SA_CMD_DIGEST_LENGTH;
 	ctx->sa_record->sa_cmd0_word |= FIELD_PREP(EIP93_SA_CMD_DIGEST_LENGTH,
